 "text": "I can't verify the exact current wording of the Act's rent-payment provisions, so please check the section against the e-Laws text before relying on this.\n\nThe clause requires the tenant to set up a pre-authorized monthly bank transfer. Ontario's Act restricts how a landlord may require rent to be paid, including by pre-authorized or post-dated payment methods. My understanding is that section 106 is the provision that addresses this, and that a term requiring a pre-authorized payment method is therefore unenforceable against an ordinary tenancy. Because the tenant agrees to it in the lease, the clause also runs into section 4, which says tenants cannot waive rights under the Act, though I'm less certain how that interacts with the specific payment rule.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 106",
